> fountain and dipped for Excalibur.
>
> Having Excalibur (at +5 due to finding some scrolls of enchant
> weapon), and +3 sdsm, what advice can you give to someone
> with moderate experience?  The farthest I have ever gotten is
> to the quest level, so I still consider myself a relative beginner.

How deep are you? What's your XL, stats, intrinsics and other
equipment?  Anyway, with +5 Excal you have exquisite damage output,
and you have a good AC (I hope you optimised your other armor
as well). The best adcvice I can give right now is to not become
overconfident and keep playing as carefully as you did before (or
more. Actually, more careful is always better). I guess Soko and the
mines have been cleared, and you found the BoH (since you wished for
SDSM)? The general way of proceeding at that stage is to make sure you
have all the critical intrinsics and equipment. You'll need poison
resistance and magic resistance at the least (though the latter is
hard to come by and _can_ wait until the next wish if it has to). Do
you have a good ranged attack up your sleeve?

Anyway, as soon as you're XL14 and have a good negative AC, it
might be time for the quest. Get fire resistance there as soon as
possible if you don't have it (there's a lot of monsters granting it
there). The Orb of Fate will effectively double your hitpoints and
grant an emergency levelport, and the valk quest isn't hard as long
as you don't typo and fall into lava, so doing it as soon as possible
is probably a good idea.

